{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Separates a string of nested parentheses groups into a list of individual balanced groups, ignoring spaces.\n    Each group is balanced and not nested within other separated groups.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    current_group = \"\"\n    balance_level = 0\n    \n    # Remove all spaces from the input string as specified.\n    cleaned_string = paren_string.replace(\" \", \"\")\n\n    for char in cleaned_string:\n        current_group += char\n        if char == '(':\n            balance_level += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance_level -= 1\n\n        # When balance_level returns to 0, a complete, top-level balanced group is found.\n        if balance_level == 0:\n            result.append(current_group)\n            current_group = \"\"\n            \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/0", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef has_close_elements(numbers: List[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Check if in given list of numbers, are any two numbers closer to each other than\n    given threshold.\n    This function iterates through all unique pairs, calculates their absolute difference, and compares it with the threshold.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    if n < 2:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # Calculate the absolute difference between two numbers.\n            distance = abs(numbers[i] - numbers[j])\n\n            # Return True if the distance is less than the threshold.\n            if distance < threshold:\n                return True\n\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/0", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef has_close_elements(numbers: List[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if in the given list of numbers, any two numbers are closer to each other\n    than the specified threshold. Returns True if a close pair is found, False otherwise.\n    \n    >>> has_close_elements([1.0, 2.0, 3.0], 0.5)\n    False\n    >>> has_close_elements([1.0, 2.8, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0, 2.0], 0.3)\n    True\n    >>> has_close_elements([], 0.1)\n    False\n    >>> has_close_elements([5.0], 0.1)\n    False\n    >>> has_close_elements([0.1, 0.2, 0.3], 0.1)\n    True\n    >>> has_close_elements([10.0, 20.0, 30.0], 0.05)\n    False\n    >>> has_close_elements([1.0, 1.0], 0.0)\n    False\n    >>> has_close_elements([1.0, 1.0], 0.0001)\n    True\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs of numbers.\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # Calculate the absolute difference and compare it with the threshold.\n            if abs(numbers[i] - numbers[j]) < threshold:\n                return True\n    return False"}
