{"task_id": "HumanEval/13", "solution": "def greatest_common_divisor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return a greatest common divisor of two integers a and b.\n    This function implements the Euclidean algorithm for GCD calculation.\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(3, 5)\n    1\n    >>> greatest_common_divisor(25, 15)\n    5\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure inputs are non-negative for the Euclidean algorithm to correctly\n    # return a positive GCD as per standard mathematical definition.\n    a = abs(a)\n    b = abs(b)\n\n    # Implement the Euclidean algorithm to find the greatest common divisor.\n    while b:\n        a, b = b, a % b\n    return a"}
