{"task_id": "HumanEval/40", "solution": "from typing import Iterator, Tuple\n\n\ndef _validate_input(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates if the input list has at least three elements.\n    This is required for forming a triplet.\n    \"\"\"\n    return len(l) >= 3\n\n\ndef _generate_triplets(l: list) -> Iterator[Tuple[int, int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates all distinct three-element combinations from the input list.\n    Elements are considered distinct by their positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    for i in range(n - 2):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n - 1):\n            for k in range(j + 1, n):\n                yield (l[i], l[j], l[k])\n\n\ndef _calculate_sum(triplet: Tuple[int, int, int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the arithmetic sum of the three elements in a given triplet.\n    It returns the sum as an integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    return triplet[0] + triplet[1] + triplet[2]\n\n\ndef triples_sum_to_zero(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    triples_sum_to_zero takes a list of integers as an input.\n    It returns True if there are three distinct elements in the list that\n    sum to zero, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_input(l):\n        return False\n\n    for triplet in _generate_triplets(l):\n        if _calculate_sum(triplet) == 0:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
