{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Returns a string representation after the conversion.\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    remainders = []\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        remainders.append(str(remainder))\n        current_x //= base\n\n    return \"\".join(remainders[::-1])"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    Return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_inputs(number: int, target_base: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates input parameters according to business rules.\n        Raises ValueError if number is negative or base is out of range [2, 9].\n        \"\"\"\n        if number < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Number to convert cannot be negative.\")\n        if not (2 <= target_base < 10):\n            raise ValueError(\"Target base must be an integer between 2 and 9 (inclusive).\")\n\n    def _convert_to_base(number: int, target_base: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Performs the mathematical base conversion algorithm using division and remainder.\n        Converts the given number to its string representation in the target base.\n        \"\"\"\n        if number == 0:\n            return \"0\"\n\n        result_digits: list[str] = []\n        current_number = number\n        while current_number > 0:\n            remainder = current_number % target_base\n            result_digits.append(str(remainder))\n            current_number //= target_base\n        \n        # The digits are collected in reverse order.\n        return \"\".join(result_digits[::-1])\n\n    _validate_inputs(x, base)\n    return _convert_to_base(x, base)\n```"}
